FirstMet: {
	Rolename1: ???
	Rolename2: Halibut
	Line0: Sir... your fishing technique... leaves something to be desired.
	Line1: You may call me Dr. Halibut.
	Line2: Or, just Halibut is fine.
	Line3: Thanks to your hook, I was pulled out of that silent, dead water.
	Line4: If it weren't for you, I'd probably have been stuck in a system crash... until I truly expired.
	Line5: This fish should have been your catch. Now, it's a gift to mark our meeting.
	Line6: ......
	Line7: You're wondering why I'm here, aren't you.
	Line8: I was a professor at the Sulphurous Sea University, Department of Abyssal Research.
	Line9: A few years ago, we organized an 'Abyssal Ecological Sampling Project.'
	Line10: I was the only one who made it back.
	Line11: At the bottom of the abyss, we encountered... an existence that cannot be understood.
	Line12: It couldn't have been a living thing, nor something that could be 'killed.' It was more like... terror, in its conceptual form.
	Line13: As I fled, I found an eye beneath a coral tree.
	Line14: On pure survival instinct, I swallowed it.
	Line15: Using the power of that eye, I opened a domain... and tore a fissure in the abyss to escape.
	Line16: After that, my memory blurs... I fell into a deep slumber, until you fished me up.
	Line17: You look like a Terrarian.
	Line18: If you'll have me, take me with you.
	Line19: I will help you conquer this land.
	Line20: In exchange... help me solve this... 'revival' problem with the eyes inside me.
	Line21: If there are no objections, let's begin by... studying this fish.
}

EyeOfCthulhuGift: {
	L0: Your movements were dragged into slow-motion... I just thought you were striking a pose.
	L1: We've entered the 'Watched Stage.' Which means... more trouble.
	L2: I found this in its... maw. Take it. A Cthulhu Fish. Just like its namesake... it doesn't really follow logic.
	L3: Hold onto it, but be careful. It'll make you think you've opened your third eye. In reality, it's just a stimulant in your bloodstream.
	L4: I'm curious if you'll start winking at the moon now.
}

KingSlimeGift: {
	L0: That blue blob... a 'slime,' you call it? Looked more like... solidified emotion.
	L1: Perhaps a clumsy attempt by matter to gain self-awareness and evolve.
	L2: Here you go, a Slimefish. Don't squeeze it. Its feelings might explode.
	L3: Have you ever tried to make soup with one of these?
	L4: I mean... yes, we can make soup at the bottom of the sea. The sea floor even has... well, seas within the sea.
}

QueenBeeGift: {
	L0: I almost got a faceful of honey back there.
	L1: Still, I managed to pull a fish out of a honey puddle on the ground.
	L2: Here, fresh and... still-warm Honeyfish.
	L3: I think it would be perfect for a sweet and sour dish.
}

SkeletronGift: {
	L0: Now that was a significant amount of calcium.
	L1: Its cranial structure reminded me of a runaway psychic construct.
	L2: Let my gun barrel cool down. I found a fish around here in the meantime.
	L3: Look, a 'Skeletron Fish.' They say the phosphorus inside makes night-fishers contemplate their existence.
	L4: Let's move. More... 'abstract' bones await.
}

AquaticScourgeGift: {
	L0: It reminds me of the less-friendly neighbors from my hometown. This one was quite amicable, though. Used to be the head of security at Sulphurous Sea University. Always said hello.
	L1: The Sulphurous Sea is an interesting place. Every creature there asks the same question: 'Why am I still alive?'
	L2: A Prismfish. Its scales refract colors you've never seen. Mainly because they shouldn't exist.
	L3: Staring at it will reboot your visual system. Like a forced update, but more painful.
	L4: Best to use it in dim light. Otherwise, you'll feel... high.
}

BrimstoneElementalGift: {
	L0: Her just standing there was like a burning speech. Good thing we managed to shut her up.
	L1: Some elementals aren't created. They're just... oddities... that seep out of the world's cracks.
	L2: An Obsidianfish. A product of instantly cooled lava. Its scales are harder than the grudges festering in hell.
	L3: Careful, it might spontaneously combust in your hand. Emotionally speaking.
	L4: After all, anger is contagious.
}

CalamitasCloneGift: {
	L0: A cheap shadow. Reminds me of the genetic monstrosities I used to cook up in my trench back in university. In any case, the one who made this has terrible taste.
	L1: I have a bad feeling. The real terror is still waiting... deeper. It's even getting closer.
	L2: Back to business. A Brimstone Fish, picked from her embers. You can still hear it muttering nonsense if you hold it close.
	L3: If you start to understand what it's saying... well, congratulations. You've taken the first step into madness.
	L4: But don't worry. Madness is just another form of clarity, seen from a different angle.
}

CrabulonGift: {
	L0: That mushroom-like... being? Is it wisdom or just pure instinct hidden under its cap?
	L1: Did you know mycelial networks can transmit information? Maybe it was calling for help.
	L2: This is a Fungifish. I barely caught it among the spores it was releasing.
	L3: Don't worry, the spores won't turn a human into a fungus... probably.
	L4: But if you suddenly get the urge to put down roots in a dark, damp place, do let me know.
}

CryogenGift: {
	L0: A frozen soul...
	L1: In the Abyssal Archives, this kind of low temperature is usually used to 'preserve' the lunatics.
	L2: A Cryo-minnow, thawed from the ice shards. It's still holding the pose it was frozen in.
	L3: They say eating it cools your blood, makes your thoughts exceptionally clear.
	L4: Eat too many, and you might just become an ice sculpture.
}

DevourerOfGodsGift: {
	L0: The Devourer of Gods... a cosmic serpent that dines on deities. Its appetite is as infinite as its ambition.
	L1: You know what they say: when you gaze into the abyss, the abyss gazes back. But this thing doesn't just gaze. It wants you for a snack.
	L2: A Neon Tetra. It floated out of a void rift. The light it emits isn't from this dimension.
	L3: Looking at it makes your brain try to comprehend colors it shouldn't. It's a... unique experience.
	L4: If you start seeing new colors, congratulations. If you start *smelling* colors, you need a rest.
}

GolemGift: {
	L0: A pile of moving rocks. Legacy of an ancient civilization... or perhaps, proof of their failure.
	L1: It might be guarding something. Or just repeating a program that lost its meaning long ago.
	L2: A Rockfish, dug from the temple's foundation. Its density makes me question my own existence.
	L3: I tried to boil it once. My pot surrendered first.
	L4: ...Some things exist just to make us realize that not all problems need to be solved.
}

HiveMindGift: {
	L0: A collective consciousness made of corruption... what a disgusting concept.
	L1: Its thought process must be... unique. Countless rotten fragments pieced together into a single, twisted whole.
	L2: Here, a Rotfish. Pulled it from that pile of carrion. Don't ask how.
	L3: It smells like seafood that's been left in the sun for three days.
	L4: But they say it lets you... resonate with the corruption. That just sounds wrong.
}

LeviathanGift: {
	L0: The ocean's tyrant... and her little sidekick who's always following her. Some friendships transcend species. And logic.
	L1: I think what lives in the deepest trenches isn't fear, it's loneliness. They're just looking for company.
	L2: A Tropic-cuda, pulled from a deep-sea vortex. It looks ordinary, which is precisely what's suspicious about it.
	L3: The more mundane the exterior, the more extraordinary the past.
	L4: Just like us.
}

MoonLordGift: {
	L0: The Lord of the Moon, ha! Or, *formerly*. Now just a floating pile of eyeballs and gore.
	L1: We didn't just save the world; we closed a door that was never meant to be opened.
	L2: I caught a Cloudfish. It floated down from a crack in the sky. Feels weightless in my hand.
	L3: They say it lets you see the future... but you've already rewritten that future.
	L4: We just proved that even gods can bleed.
}

PerforatorGift: {
	L0: A pile of drilling flesh-worms... this creature's existence is a challenge to biology.
	L1: Their blood has a strange viscosity, like some kind of living metal.
	L2: Found this in the wreckage. A Gore-fish. It's still wriggling.
	L3: Don't be scared by its looks, even if it looks like it crawled out of a nightmare.
	L4: At least it won't crawl into your ear while you sleep... probably.
}

PlaguebringerGift: {
	L0: The Plaguebringer... a mechanical bee carrying a bioweapon. Who designed this? A real bastard, daring to enslave bees.
	L1: A virus doesn't care about right or wrong. It just wants to survive. Like us, only more direct.
	L2: A Jewel-fish. Infected and miraculously recovered. Its immune system is more experienced than you are.
	L3: They say eating it boosts resistance. Sounds like another way of saying 'what doesn't kill you makes you stronger.'
	L4: But since *we* just walked out of a plague-hive, this little risk should be nothing.
}

PlanteraGift: {
	L0: A flower... if 'flower' is the word for that man-eating vine conglomerate.
	L1: The jungle's rage, grown in plant form. Nature's revenge is never rational.
	L2: A Twin-Cod. It has two heads. The jungle is like a land-ocean; things here don't need a reason to grow extra parts.
	L3: They say two heads mean twice the wisdom, but they just look like they're arguing over which way to swim.
	L4: Like 'diet' and 'appetite.' Always fighting. My appetite always wins, though.
}

ProvidenceGift: {
	L0: The Profaned Goddess... a contradiction of faith and flame. Quite pitiful.
	L1: We didn't just extinguish a holy flame, but the embers of an entire era.
	L2: A Demon-Hell Fish, reborn from her ashes. Its temperature is permanently fixed at 'just hot enough not to burn you.'
	L3: That precise control makes me suspect... maybe she just wanted to be understood.
	L4: But the line between understanding and war is only one attack away.
}

SlimeGodGift: {
	L0: Three slimes... or, a fractured divinity? This dualistic existence is... interesting.
	L1: Corruption and Crimson. The eternal conflict of this world. And we just proved that conflict can be 'resolved.'
	L2: A Variegated Lardfish. Scooped from the goo. Don't ask about the name.
	L3: Its color changes with the observer's mood. Or perhaps, it's mimicking your inner chaos.
	L4: Stare too long, and you might start to wonder which side you're really on.
}

SupremeCalamitasGift: {
	L0: Brimstone Witch... an avenger. The most powerful magic-wielder of the last century.
	L1: What we just did... did we end a legend, or create a new one?
	L2: A Princessfish, born from her embers. It has a conflicting grace, like a flower blooming in ruins.
	L3: They say it shows you the person you most want to be... but that version is often the least like yourself.
	L4: You're nearing the peak of Terrarian power. From here on... it's a long way down.
}

WallOfFleshGift: {
	L0: A wall of flesh and bone... this world's creator must have had some peculiar ideas.
	L1: You just broke some kind of balance. Feel that? The world's pulse is quickening.
	L2: Found this Hungering Fish in the remains. It looks eternally starved.
	L3: Just like that wall. Always chasing, always consuming.
	L4: Welcome to 'Hard Mode'... though I didn't think it was 'easy' before.
}

YharonGift: {
	L0: The Jungle Dragon... no, the World-Burning Dragon. It burns not with flesh, but with obsession.
	L1: A loyalty so pure it would burn itself to ash for its master... reminds me of the fish schools that guard the coral reefs back home.
	L2: A Scarlet Tigerfish. Just caught it. I'm quite fond of its stripes.
	L3: Holding it, you feel a scorching resolve. That is the temperature of a warrior.
	L4: You defeated that dragon, but I have to wonder... in the moment it fell, did it finally find... release?
}

ResurrectionWarn: {
	Line0: Wait... did you feel that?
	Line1: The 'resurrection' state is approaching a critical threshold.
	Line2: I have to warn you, this isn't a game.
	Line3: If the resurrection completes... the consequences will be dire.
	Line4: The end result... is being consumed by the abyss.
	Line5: Every one of these eyes that opens inside me... it accelerates the resurrection process.
	Line6: The more that are open, the faster it builds, and the greater the danger.
	Line7: This is the price for wielding abyssal power. If I don't have the eyes open, my own abilities are severely diminished.
	Line8: We need to learn how to balance it—to determine how many eyes are 'safe' to have open during combat.
	Line9: If we want to use this power without consequence...
	Line10: ...we have to find a way to make these eyes 'crash.'
}

FishoilQuestScenario: {
	Line0: You seem to have caught a fair amount of common fish recently.
	Line1: Give me some for my research, and I can refine them into a bottle of fresh fish oil.
	Line2: The process isn't difficult, just... tedious.
	Line3: This fish oil has potential. It's more useful than you might think.
	Line4: Interested?
	ChoiceAccept: Alright.
	ChoiceDecline: Not interested.
}

HelensInterference: {
	Line0: ...Hey, are you free?
	Line1: Today..... uh.... nice weather, right?
	Line2: (Halibut seems to be hiding something.)
	Question1: ......
	Choice1_1: What are you doing?
	Choice1_2: Hand it over!
	Choice1_3: (Say nothing)
	FinalQuestion: Don't go any further... please. That witch, her commissions, the things she wants... I don't want to see it. We can walk the rest of the path ourselves, can't we?
	FinalChoice_Continue: Continue the commission
	FinalChoice_Stop: Stop the commission

	Branch_Anger: {
		Line1: ...You really... trust her *that* much?
		Line2: Haven't you noticed? The things that witch gives you... none of them are normal.
		Line3: It reminds me of something... in the Abyss... I... I touched it... cold, terrifying, unsettling... Ugh... I don't want to remember.
		Line4: You should have realized this...
	}

	Branch_Inquiry: {
		Line1: I've been getting more and more anxious lately.
		Line2: That blade... when I touched it, I thought I heard... someone *laughing*.
		Line3: They all feel like... some kind of 'conduit'.
		Line4: I can't let you go on with it, at least...
	}

	Branch_Silence: {
		Line1: ...You're most terrifying when you're silent.
		Line2: ...Fine, I hid the Heartcarver.
		Line3: That witch... she's dangerous, she came from nowhere. If this is a trap, are you just going to walk right into it?
		Line4: Stop... please. For my sake.
	}

	FinalBranch_Continue: {
		Line1: ...Fine. I knew you'd choose this.
		Line2: ......
		Line3: I'll put it back. But I hope... when you use it... you'll be careful.
		Line4: And that witch, too...
		Line5: I'll walk with you... all the way.
	}

	FinalBranch_Stop: {
		Line1: ...You're... you're really willing to stop?
		Line2: ......
		Line3: Let's go. Let that witch go to hell.
	}
}

HellGift: {
	L0: This damn place... Hell is getting hotter and hotter.
	L1: I have an idea. Let's just dig through the sea floor and make this part of the ocean, too.
	L2: A geothermal hot spring... spanning the entire continent.
	L3: ...Just thinking about it is relaxing.
	L4: Oh, right. I caught a fish.
	L5: At first, I thought it was a guide for the hell-springs, but... it just looks like one.
}

DyeProtest: {
	L1: Honestly, I don't really like wearing those bright colors.
	L2: Get it washed off, will you? Put it in the dye vat, then use that water bucket.
}

FishoilSubmitScenario: {
	SubmitLine1: Hmm, you've collected enough fish.
	SubmitLine2: Just enough for me to extract a bottle of fish oil.
	QuestionLine: Are you going to hand them over to me?
	ChoiceGive: Sure, take them.
	ChoiceRefuse: Let me think about it.
	GiveResponse: Excellent, just a moment... Here you go, a fresh bottle of fish oil.
	RefuseResponse: Alright, come find me whenever you've made up your mind.
	QuestTitle: Fish Oil Collection
	QuestSummary: Collect 300 ordinary fish and give them to Halibut in exchange for a bottle of fish oil.
	QuestCategory: Halibut
	ProgressFormat: "{0}/{1}"
	TrackerCollecting: "{0} more fish needed"
	TrackerReady: Fish collected. Please focus on the quest to submit.
	StatusSuspended: Suspended
	StatusCompleted: Completed
	StatusSubmittable: Ready to Submit
	StatusCollectingFormat: Collecting ({0}/{1})
	NotEnoughResponse: Hmm? It seems you don't have enough fish. Go catch some more and come back.
	AlreadyCompletedResponse: I've already given you the fish oil. If you want more, you'll have to wait until next time.
	SubmitButtonLabel: Submit Fish
	AwaitingSubmitHint: Click submit to give the fish to Halibut
}

GeiGeiEasterEgg: {
	L0: That battle was truly perilous.
	L1: But the records tell of a warrior from back then called Gei-Gei, who was far more terrifying.
}
